[stderr] # 04 — Audio direction
[stderr] 
[stderr] Audio is original, optional, captioned/described where it conveys state, and
[stderr] always paired with a visual/text equivalent. No chant, anthem, broadcast,
[stderr] club, or game imitation is permitted.
[stderr] 
[stderr] Final durations, quantities, loudness targets, loop policy, and generated-cue
[stderr] selection need production approval; no audio is generated by this plan.
[stderr] 
[stderr] ## Original-audio contract and cue IDs
[stderr] 
[stderr] Audio reinforces the original *matchday knowledge* arc: invitation, confident
[stderr] answer, rising streak, decisive result, and clear return. It shares the abstract
[stderr] broadcast-studio vocabulary of `01-creative-direction.md` and the journey map
[stderr] in `04-experience-contract.md`: bright electronic percussion, soft claps, warm
[stderr] brass-like synth accents, and abstract crowd-energy texture. It is not a real
[stderr] crowd, chant, anthem, commentary, broadcaster ident, club sound, football-game
[stderr] imitation, or vocal performance associated with a real team.
[stderr] 
[stderr] Cue IDs use `AUDIO-<FAMILY>-<NNN>` and are immutable after package reference.
[stderr] Rendered variants append `-<state>-<mix>`; a manifest records ID, source-session
[stderr] or render checksum, creator/provenance, licence, loop points, loudness/peak,
[stderr] duration, caption/description key, trigger, mix group, and review state.
[stderr] Essential state also has text, icon/pattern, and semantic announcement. Captions
[stderr] describe function (for example, “brief rising streak cue”); missing audio never
[stderr] blocks an action.
[stderr] 
[stderr] P0 is instrumental only: no intelligible vocals, sampled speech, commentary,
[stderr] chants, crowd recordings, or copyrighted musical imitation. Original/properly
[stderr] licensed sources only; generated cues retain settings and receive human
[stderr] originality review.
[stderr] 
[stderr] | Stable ID | Purpose, journey, and trigger | Target loop / duration | Acceptance and accessibility |
[stderr] | --- | --- | --- | --- |
[stderr] | `AUDIO-MUS-001` | Home/round-choice invitation bed; J0/J2 after screen settles. | Seamless 20–40 s loop with clean entry/exit. | Low-distraction music; mute/fade immediately; never masks UI feedback or speech. |
[stderr] | `AUDIO-QZ-001` | Prompt-ready tick; J1/J2 when an unresolved card is actionable. | One-shot ≤0.5 s. | Caption “Question ready”; visible/announced card is complete without it. |
[stderr] | `AUDIO-QZ-002` | Correct confirmation; J1/J2 after adjudication. | One-shot ≤0.8 s. | Caption “Correct cue”; distinguishable from incorrect without pitch alone; never precedes written result. |
[stderr] | `AUDIO-QZ-003` | Incorrect correction; J1/J2 after adjudication. | One-shot ≤0.8 s. | Caption “Answer correction cue”; calm/non-punitive; explanation remains primary. |
[stderr] | `AUDIO-QZ-004` | Streak threshold rise; J1/J2 on confirmed 3+ streak. | One-shot ≤1.2 s. | Caption “Streak rises”; one per card; suppressible under reduced feedback. |
[stderr] | `AUDIO-RES-001` | Results sting; J1/J2 when results first appear. | One-shot 2–4 s, never loops. | Caption “Round complete”; controls available immediately and meaningful muted. |
[stderr] | `AUDIO-SET-001` | Player-requested settings preview; J0 after audio preference change. | One-shot ≤0.5 s. | Obeys current volume/mute; visible labelled test control; never autoplays on Settings open. |
[stderr] | `AUDIO-SYS-001` | Package update ready/applied; J5 at a between-round state only. | One-shot ≤0.7 s. | Caption “Update ready/applied”; visible keyboard-accessible status/action. |
[stderr] | `AUDIO-SYS-002` | Save/recovery attention; J3 when recovery panel appears. | One-shot ≤0.7 s. | Caption “Save attention cue”; non-alarming, non-looping, never replaces recovery choices. |
[stderr] 
[stderr] ## Playback and mixing policy
[stderr] 
[stderr] Provide persistent per-local-profile master mute and independent music/feedback
[stderr] controls. Honour platform/system volume, audio focus/interruption, and exposed
[stderr] reduced-sensory preferences. Backgrounding pauses nonessential playback and
[stderr] never affects game state. Do not autoplay audible music before player
[stderr] interaction where platform policy requires it.
[stderr] 
[stderr] The same IDs serve responsive web, PWA, Android, and iPhone. Web/PWA waits for
[stderr] audio unlock and silently retains captions/text if unavailable; phones respect
[stderr] mute switch/audio focus. Keyboard, touch, mouse, and gamepad invoke the same
[stderr] semantic state and therefore the same cue. Remote/TV delivery is out of P0.
[stderr] 
[stderr] Production tests cover speakers/headphones, system muted, audio unavailable,
[stderr] screen-reader speech, interruption, offline cached assets, and reduced feedback.
[stderr] Acceptance requires intended trigger once at safe state, correct loop/duration,
[stderr] no required audio-only meaning, caption key, mute/volume support, permitted
[stderr] source, and complete manifest provenance/checksum/review. Exact final rendered
[stderr] count, loudness readings, formats, size budget, and language captions await
[stderr] production approval; this plan creates or licenses no audio.
[stderr] # 03 — Technical, data, trust, and quality contract
[stderr] 
[stderr] **Inputs:** [`INITIAL.md`](../INITIAL.md), [domain discovery](00-domain-discovery.md),
[stderr] [game identity](01-game-identity.md), [creative direction](01-creative-direction.md),
[stderr] [feature model](02-feature-model.md), and [game design bible](02-game-design-bible.md).
[stderr] 
[stderr] This contract implements the bounded first-release football-trivia game. It
[stderr] does not turn the brief's approval-gated account, multiplayer, live-service,
[stderr] commerce, or remote-sync requests into production scope. It specifies a
[stderr] vendor-neutral architecture so those systems can be added only after their
[stderr] identity, cost, safety, retention, and outage decisions are approved.
[stderr] 
[stderr] ## Production architecture and boundaries
[stderr] 
[stderr] The release is an offline-capable 2D client game with one shared deterministic
[stderr] domain core, immutable validated content packages, platform adapters, and local
[stderr] durable storage. The initial web/PWA and Android/iOS outputs package the same
[stderr] core and content; a platform adapter may render, persist, cache, map inputs,
[stderr] report a fault locally, or obtain an approved release, but cannot adjudicate an
[stderr] answer or alter a score. The core has no renderer, platform API, clock, network,
[stderr] or third-party-service dependency.
[stderr] 
[stderr] | Component / owned boundary | Product or quality requirement traced | Contract |
[stderr] | --- | --- | --- |
[stderr] | Quiz application shell | GAME-005/008/009; J0–J3 | Owns routes, focus, pause/visibility prompts, ephemeral UI and accessible rendering. Sends intents to the core and never mutates a run directly. |
[stderr] | Input and accessibility adapters | GAME-009/012; responsive web and phones | Map touch, pointer, keyboard, and gamepad to semantic actions (`navigate`, `select`, `submit`, `back`, `pause`). Apply text/contrast/reduced-motion/caption settings; unsupported hardware has a visible equivalent. |
[stderr] | Deterministic quiz core | GAME-001, 003, 005–008 | Owns selection, normalisation/adjudication, score/streak, milestones, legal lifecycle transitions, and versioned rule calculations. Explicit seed and rule version make selection/results reproducible. |
[stderr] | Content registry and validator | GAME-001–004; curated original bank | Resolves immutable published packages by stable ID and refuses invalid or withdrawn content before it can enter a new round. Runtime reads only validated data. |
[stderr] | Save/recovery repository | GAME-008/010; J3 | Owns revisioned snapshots, checksum/validation, atomic promotion, rollback, migration, quarantine, export only if later approved, and confirmed deletion. |
[stderr] | Release/cache manager | GAME-011/012; PWA/mobile offline delivery | Stages signed/hashed approved package and assets; activates only between rounds and never during a save commit. It retains a known-good compatible package on update failure. |
[stderr] | Error boundary and diagnostics | crash recovery and privacy | Owns plain-language retry, return-home, and recovery choices. P0 diagnostics are local and consent-gated; no telemetry transport is assumed. |
[stderr] | Editorial build tooling | J4/J5; factual/release integrity | Imports author-controlled source files, runs schema/relationship/provenance checks, and emits a content manifest. It has no runtime authoring or publishing endpoint. |
[stderr] 
[stderr] ```text
[stderr] authored content ─> build validator ─> immutable ContentPackage ─┐
[stderr]                                                                ├─> deterministic quiz core <─ semantic input actions
[stderr] platform renderer/accessibility <─ state + events ─────────────┘             │
[stderr]              │                                                               ├─> save/recovery repository
[stderr]              └─> release/cache manager (safe boundary only) ─────────────────┴─> local error/diagnostic record
[stderr] ```
[stderr] 
[stderr] Only the core creates durable game facts. The shell owns transient selection,
[stderr] focus, animation and open-panel state. The repository owns serialized records,
[stderr] not gameplay. Content/cache, diagnostics, and UI must not be prerequisites for
[stderr] a legal answer, score, or completed tutorial.
[stderr] 
[stderr] ## Data, editorial content, and lifecycle contracts
[stderr] 
[stderr] | Data class | Owner and lifecycle | Local persistence/retention | Access, recovery, and authorization |
[stderr] | --- | --- | --- | --- |
[stderr] | `ContentPackage` | Editorial owner: draft → review → published → staged → active → superseded/rolled back/withdrawn | Bundled or cached immutable release artifact; current compatible and last-known-good package follow platform cache policy | Player runtime reads only published package. No content write API, account role, or remote publish service exists in P0. |
[stderr] | `LocalProfile`, settings | Player: new → active → deletion-pending → deleted; settings valid → applied → reset | Separate local records; retained until explicit profile deletion | Browser/device profile controls local access. Failed setting write retains the applied session value and explains it. |
[stderr] | `RoundRun`, attempts, results, milestones | Core: created → active/paused → complete, abandoned, or recoverable; attempts presented → draft → submitted → resolved | Valid confirmed snapshots plus prior known-good revision; unresolved draft is disposable | Immutable resolved attempts reference exact content/rule versions. A player may recover/discard only their local state. |
[stderr] | `SaveSnapshot`/recovery record | Repository: candidate → validated → confirmed → superseded/quarantined → deleted | Current confirmed revision and prior valid revision; recovery metadata is bounded and deleted with profile | No overwrite of a valid revision by a malformed candidate. Corruption/migration failure offers last valid snapshot or new game. |
[stderr] | Original visual/audio assets and strings | Creative/content owner: source → provenance/review → manifest reference → packaged → superseded | Versioned content package references; source provenance retained in repository/release records | Runtime may resolve only manifest IDs. Missing optional cue gives text feedback; missing required asset rejects release. |
[stderr] | Diagnostic record | Player-controlled: fault → local bounded record → cleared/exported only if later approved | Default no transport; bounded local retention and clear control | Excludes prompts, typed answers, profile identifiers and save content. Consent is required before recording any optional diagnostic. |
[stderr] 
[stderr] ### Versioned question, feedback, and asset schema
[stderr] 
[stderr] High-volume creative content is a first-class build input. Generated packages
[stderr] are never hand-edited, and stable IDs are never reused for a different fact.
[stderr] 
[stderr] ```text
[stderr] ContentPackage {
[stderr]   packageId, semanticVersion, schemaVersion, defaultLocale, ruleVersion,
[stderr]   cards[], roundDefinitions[], categories[], strings[], visualAssets[], audioCues[],
[stderr]   provenanceRecords[], reviewRecords[], manifestHash, compatibility
[stderr] }
[stderr] QuestionCard {
[stderr]   id, revision, status, format, promptKey, answerRule, explanationKey,
[stderr]   categoryId, era, competitionScopes[], difficultyBand, tags[], provenanceId,
[stderr]   reviewIds[], visualAssetIds[], audioCueIds[], localeCoverage
[stderr] }
[stderr] AnswerRule { canonicalIds[] | canonicalBoolean | orderedIds[] | typedAliases[] }
[stderr] AudioCue { id, revision, trigger, captionKey, durationClass, provenanceId, optional }
[stderr] VisualAsset { id, revision, kind, sourceHash, altKey, provenanceId }
[stderr] SaveSnapshot {
[stderr]   schemaVersion, contentPackageId, contentVersion, ruleVersion, profileId,
[stderr]   revision, status, selectionSeed, roundRun, attempts[], scoreState,
[stderr]   milestones, repeatLedger, settingsRef, checksum, committedAt
[stderr] }
[stderr] ```
[stderr] 
[stderr] `QB-A-01…48` and `TUT-01…05` are reserved stable card IDs; a correction creates
[stderr] a new card revision and correction history rather than silently changing an
[stderr] old run. Prompts, options, canonical answer labels, explanations, categories,
[stderr] captions, cue descriptions, asset alt text, and UI copy are localisation keys.
[stderr] An offered locale must supply reviewed strings and valid typed-answer aliases;
[stderr] otherwise it is unavailable, not partially substituted. Audio trigger names
[stderr] (`prompt_arrival`, `correct`, `incorrect`, `streak_rise`, `saved`, `results`)
[stderr] are data IDs, with caption/text equivalents and mute/volume behaviour; audio
[stderr] never carries essential information alone.
[stderr] 
[stderr] ### Editorial ownership, validation, import/export, and reference integrity
[stderr] 
[stderr] - The designated editorial owner creates original card sources; factual source
[stderr]   and rights/provenance record, checked date, accessibility/copy review, and
[stderr]   two reviewer IDs are required to publish. Uncertain rights or disputed facts
[stderr]   block the card. No scraping, copied question, unreviewed AI fact, or runtime
[stderr]   authoring/import is allowed.
[stderr] - The build import path is repository-controlled structured source → validator
[stderr]   → immutable package/manifest. A future editor may produce that source only if
[stderr]   it preserves schemas, stable IDs, review/provenance, deterministic export,
[stderr]   and the same validator. Player save export/import is not a P0 feature; any
[stderr]   later import must use a versioned envelope, size bounds, parse-before-write,
[stderr]   confirmation, and preserve the valid save on failure.
[stderr] - Validation rejects duplicate IDs/aliases, unpublished/withdrawn cards,
[stderr]   absent review/provenance/localisation keys, invalid format-specific answer
[stderr]   rules, missing assets/captions, unsupported cue trigger, invalid references,
[stderr]   incomplete compatibility declaration, and package hash mismatch. It enforces
[stderr]   GAME-002 totals/distribution/caps and GAME-006 format/difficulty adjacency
[stderr]   capability before release.
[stderr] - Relationship tests prove every round references eligible cards, every card
[stderr]   resolves its answer/explanation/category/assets/cues/provenance/reviews, each
[stderr]   alias has one intended canonical answer within a locale, and withdrawn cards
[stderr]   cannot appear in new selection. Fixed fixtures cover TUT-01…05, representative
[stderr]   cards of each format, aliases/diacritics/blanks/ambiguity, shortages, a bad
[stderr]   reference of every class, and a corrected old-content run.
[stderr] - Package compatibility declares supported save-schema, content-schema, and
[stderr]   rule-version ranges. An old snapshot continues to display its referenced
[stderr]   explanation where its package is retained; unsupported data is quarantined,
[stderr]   never guessed or rewritten. Content can activate only between rounds.
[stderr] 
[stderr] ## Commands, validation, idempotency, and concurrency
[stderr] 
[stderr] The core accepts typed intents: `CreateProfile`, `StartTutorial`, `StartRound`,
[stderr] `SelectAnswer`, `EnterTypedAnswer`, `ConfirmBlank`, `SubmitAnswer`, `Pause`,
[stderr] `Resume`, `CompleteRound`, `CommitSnapshot`, `RecoverSnapshot`, `DeleteProfile`,
[stderr] and `ApplySettings`. Each state-changing intent carries `expectedRevision` and
[stderr] a unique `interactionId`, and returns a typed rejection or ordered state/events
[stderr] with a new revision.
[stderr] 
[stderr] - Before mutation validate command shape/size, active lifecycle state,
[stderr]   expected revision, content/rule compatibility, card eligibility, selected
[stderr]   option or typed-answer normalisation, and required safe-boundary condition.
[stderr]   Treat UI events, deep links, cached content and persisted bytes as untrusted.
[stderr] - Typed answers use the GAME-003 deterministic Unicode/case/punctuation/
[stderr]   whitespace/diacritic normalisation and configured aliases only—never fuzzy
[stderr]   matching. Blank needs explicit confirmation; a resolved submission is
[stderr]   immutable and shows canonical answer/explanation.
[stderr] - `interactionId`, completed-run ID, milestone key and snapshot revision form
[stderr]   idempotency keys. Retried submission/complete/snapshot returns its recorded
[stderr]   result; it never adds score, streak, milestone, or history twice. A replay is
[stderr]   a new run with a new selection seed.
[stderr] - Process one intent per local profile/run. Disable/debounce submit while it is
[stderr]   pending and reject an old revision after asynchronous persistence completes.
[stderr]   A second browser tab or resumed process acquires a local lease or becomes
[stderr]   read-only; a stale writer cannot replace the latest confirmed revision.
[stderr] - Selection uses an explicit deterministic seed with content/rule version and
[stderr]   local repeat ledger recorded in the snapshot. The last two completed rounds
[stderr]   are excluded where possible; a shortage is a disclosed deterministic result,
[stderr]   not a hidden reroll.
[stderr] 
[stderr] ## Persistence, migrations, and failure semantics
[stderr] 
[stderr] At tutorial completion, every resolved-question boundary, explicit pause, and
[stderr] completed result, save by: serialize a candidate → validate schema/checksum/
[stderr] invariants → write immutable revision → read back/validate → atomically promote
[stderr] current pointer → retain prior known-good revision. Storage must provide an
[stderr] atomic final pointer or emulate one with revision records. It must never clear
[stderr] the previous confirmed snapshot before promotion succeeds.
[stderr] 
[stderr] | Condition | Required player-safe behaviour |
[stderr] | --- | --- |
[stderr] | Quota, permission denial, unavailable storage | Keep round playable, retain previous confirmed snapshot, state that saving failed, and offer retry/continue without saving. |
[stderr] | Process death/interrupted write | Ignore incomplete candidate; load prior confirmed revision and offer the normal resume state. |
[stderr] | Corrupt/checksum-invalid draft or snapshot | Quarantine bytes/metadata without overwrite; offer last known-good snapshot, discard draft, or new local profile. |
[stderr] | Unsupported schema or migration failure | Preserve original candidate, fail closed into quarantine, and offer explicit recovery/new-game path. |
[stderr] | Invalid/partial content/cache update | Keep compatible active package and save; block affected new-round route with retry/home explanation. Never activate it mid-round. |
[stderr] | First offline visit/no cached package | Explain that initial approved download is needed; never misrepresent an uncached game as offline-ready. |
[stderr] | Fault/crash loop | Error boundary offers retry, return home, and recovery; optional local diagnostics do not block either action. |
[stderr] | Explicit deletion | Confirm scope, then remove profile/settings/history/snapshots/recovery records/local diagnostics and return to first launch. |
[stderr] 
[stderr] Migrations are pure, ordered `fromSchema → toSchema` transformations with
[stderr] fixtures for each supported predecessor. They run into a new candidate,
[stderr] validate before promotion, and are idempotent or record source version so a
[stderr] retry cannot apply one twice. A migration cannot reinterpret old answer facts,
[stderr] grant new score/milestones, or change a completed run's content/rule reference.
[stderr] 
