[stderr] Run an entire collection once, including any new runbooks created by accepted
[stderr] tasks during the run:
[stderr] 
[stderr] ```bash
[stderr] supervisor-run --run-all --runbooks-dir ../../runbooks --initial ../../projects/my-project/INITIAL.md
[stderr] ```
[stderr] 
[stderr] Use `--initial PATH` when the brief belongs to a named project rather than the
[stderr] reusable runbook collection. Supervisor reads that file first and appends its
[stderr] context to every task. Without the flag, it looks for `INITIAL.md` in the
[stderr] collection; a generated collection can instead inherit its parent project's
[stderr] `PROJECT_BRIEF.md`. It re-enumerates the collection after each accepted wave,
[stderr] so bounded planning or authoring tasks can safely create the next wave without
[stderr] the operator restarting Supervisor.
[stderr] 
[stderr] For intentionally chained collections, add a JSON registration beneath the
[stderr] parent collection:
[stderr] 
[stderr] ```text
[stderr] <runbooks-dir>/.supervisor-children/<name>.json
[stderr] ```
[stderr] 
[stderr] ```json
[stderr] {"runbooks_dir": "../path-to-child-runbooks"}
[stderr] ```
[stderr] 
[stderr] After the parent completes, `--run-all` follows each registered child collection
[stderr] recursively. This is explicit by design: Supervisor never scans and executes
[stderr] arbitrary directories. Named-project collection state is stored in that
[stderr] workspace's `.state/` directory, so generated task IDs such as `R0001` remain
[stderr] isolated across projects. Set `SUPERVISOR_DATABASE_PATH` only when deliberately
[stderr] sharing state.
[stderr] 
[stderr] ## Updating project configuration safely
[stderr] 
[stderr] `supervisor update` fast-forwards the project-owned `supervisor/` checkout,
[stderr] reinstalls its CLI, then runs the newly downloaded version's environment
[stderr] migrations. The authoritative, append-only history is committed to the
[stderr] Supervisor repository in `supervisor/env_migrations.json`. `supervisor update`
[stderr] compares that manifest with `SUPERVISOR_ENV_SCHEMA_VERSION` in the project's
[stderr] private project-root `.env`, adds missing safe defaults or declared renamed keys, and never
