[stderr] +# 05 — Delivery map
[stderr] +
[stderr] +**Inputs:** discovery, game identity/bible, creative/asset/audio direction,
[stderr] +technical contract, and [production inventory](game-production-inventory.md).
[stderr] +The repository currently contains specifications and Supervisor tooling, not an
[stderr] +application source tree. Paths below are deliberate future ownership boundaries,
[stderr] +not claims that code already exists. Complete the gated G design collection
[stderr] +before F006; never substitute placeholders for `GPI-*` content or creative IDs.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Planned layout and dependency rule
[stderr] +
[stderr] +```text
[stderr] +src/core/       deterministic quiz, content, scoring, lifecycle and save rules
[stderr] +src/content/    authored QB/TUT sources, schemas, provenance and validators
[stderr] +src/platform/   web/PWA and native-wrapper input, storage, cache, audio adapters
[stderr] +src/app/        accessible responsive shell, views, settings, feedback
[stderr] +assets/         original visual/audio source, manifests and reviewed renders
[stderr] +tests/          core, content, platform, app and release evidence
[stderr] +docs/           editorial, accessibility, privacy, support and release evidence
[stderr] +```
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Each `PW-*` path is reserved exclusively for its row. Target budgets, framework,
[stderr] +store accounts, signing, and service vendors remain approval gates; the shared
[stderr] +offline client may proceed without inventing them.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Shared foundations and real creative inputs
[stderr] +
[stderr] +| ID | Bounded outcome | Depends on | Owns files/data | Verification |
[stderr] +| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
[stderr] +| DM-01 | Bootstrap selected client framework, deterministic tests, lint/format, and directory boundaries. | stack approval | root config; `src/`; `tests/`; `docs/development.md` | Clean bootstrap and sample pure-core test. |
[stderr] +| DM-02 | Implement immutable commands/events/state, revisions, interaction IDs, seeded RNG, and invariants without platform imports. | DM-01 | `src/core/{state,commands,events,invariants,rng}` | Unit tests reject stale/illegal commands without mutation. |
[stderr] +| DM-03 | Implement versioned content schema/import validator and immutable package manifest. | DM-01–02; GPI-001 | `src/content/{schema,validator,registry}`; `content/`; `tests/content/` | Valid minimal package passes; one negative fixture per reference/status failure fails. |
[stderr] +| DM-04 | Produce and validate GPI-001 plus all four named Kickoff Mix batches GPI-002–005, including two-review and rights/source records. | DM-03; accepted G evidence | `content/cards/`; `content/provenance/`; `tests/content/editorial.*` | 48-card quota/cap/source/review/locale validator report. |
[stderr] +| DM-05 | Produce and validate TUT-01–05, GPI-008, as a fixed accessible offline tutorial package. | DM-03–04; accepted G evidence | `content/tutorial/`; tutorial fixtures | Every named card resolves and tutorial fixture completes once. |
[stderr] +| DM-06 | Implement GPI-006 adjudication and GPI-007 eligibility/anti-repeat policy. | DM-02–04; accepted G evidence | `src/core/{answer,selection}`; fixtures | Alias/blank/ambiguous/withdrawn and seeded-shortage tests. |
[stderr] +| DM-07 | Create original P0 visual sources for `ASSET-SHL/QZ/UI/FBK/SYS-001` families, variants, alt/meaning records, checksums, and review ledger. | DM-03; GPI-001, 008–014 | `assets/visual/`; `assets/manifest.*`; `tests/content/assets.*` | Provenance, contrast, 200%/high-contrast/reduced-motion and missing-asset checks. |
[stderr] +| DM-08 | Generate/select original P0 `AUDIO-*` cues, captions/descriptions, manifests, accessibility fallbacks, and provenance/review records. | DM-03; accepted G evidence | `assets/audio/`; `assets/audio-manifest.*`; `tests/content/audio.*` | Trigger/caption/mute/duration/checksum/licence validation; no audio-only meaning. |
[stderr] +| DM-09 | Implement content/asset/audio registry resolving only reviewed manifest IDs and safe optional-media fallback. | DM-03–08 | `src/content/{assets,audio,package}`; integration fixtures | Missing optional media falls back; missing required/package-invalid media rejects new round. |
[stderr] +| DM-10 | Implement revisioned confirmed local snapshot repository, migration runner, quarantine/delete, and local consent-gated diagnostics. | DM-02–03 | `src/core/save/`; `src/platform/storage/`; `tests/{core,platform}/save.*` | Fault injection preserves last confirmed save and excludes prompt/answer payloads. |
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Core quiz features and UI/input integration
[stderr] +
[stderr] +| ID | Bounded outcome | Depends on | Owns files/data | Verification |
[stderr] +| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
[stderr] +| DM-11 | Implement First Whistle lifecycle and one-time local milestone from GPI-008. | DM-02, 05–06, 10 | `src/core/tutorial/`; `tests/core/tutorial.*` | Offline start, resolve, restart, and idempotent milestone tests. |
[stderr] +| DM-12 | Implement Mixed Fixture lifecycle and GPI-009 deterministic eligible 10-card selection. | DM-02, 04, 06, 10 | `src/core/round/`; `tests/core/round.*` | Seeded selection, optional timer, pause, shortage and safe-boundary tests. |
[stderr] +| DM-13 | Implement GPI-010 score/streak and GPI-011 result events with explainable feedback. | DM-06, 12 | `src/core/{score,results}`; fixtures | Cap/reset/blank/abandon/non-decreasing/idempotent-complete tests. |
[stderr] +| DM-14 | Build responsive semantic shell: profile, home, tutorial/round entry, pause, results, error boundary, and focus/visibility state. | DM-01, 10–13 | `src/app/{shell,navigation,recovery}`; `PW-14-shell.spec.*` | App tests; `supervisor/browser/tests/changes/pw-14-shell.spec.*` covers no-save, resume, reflow and focus return. |
[stderr] +| DM-15 | Build card, choice, typed-answer, confirm, explanation, score/streak, and result surfaces wired to real GPI content and media IDs. | DM-07–09, 11–14 | `src/app/{quiz,feedback,results}`; `PW-15-round.spec.*` | State-driven tests; `PW-15` completes tutorial and standard round with media unavailable. |
[stderr] +| DM-16 | Map touch, pointer, keyboard, and feature-detected gamepad to one semantic action vocabulary. | DM-02, 14 | `src/platform/input/`; `src/app/controls/`; `PW-16-input.spec.*` | Adapter fixtures; `PW-16` checks keyboard-only, touch, pointer and unavailable gamepad. |
[stderr] +| DM-17 | Implement GPI-012 settings/accessibility: scale/spacing/contrast, captions, reduced motion/sensory feedback, visible focus, labels, dialogs and locale fallback. | DM-08, 12, 14–16 | `src/app/{settings,accessibility,i18n}`; `PW-17-accessibility.spec.*` | Automated scan plus `PW-17` 200% reflow, caption/mute, contrast, reduced-motion and focus tests. |
[stderr] +| DM-18 | Integrate GPI-013 recovery panels and snapshot coordination at resolved, pause, and result boundaries. | DM-10–15 | `src/app/recovery/`; `src/core/session/`; `PW-18-recovery.spec.*` | Fault tests; `PW-18` shows write-failure, corruption and confirmed-delete choices. |
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Target adapters, operations, trust, release, and evidence
[stderr] +
[stderr] +| ID | Bounded outcome | Depends on | Owns files/data | Verification |
[stderr] +| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
[stderr] +| DM-19 | Implement responsive-web/PWA adapter: manifest, install, cache, offline status, known-good retention, and between-round update gate. | DM-04, 09–10, 14–18 | `public/`; `src/platform/{web,pwa}`; `PW-19-pwa.spec.*` | `PW-19` covers uncached explanation, cached play, install unavailable, deferred update and failed refresh retention. |
[stderr] +| DM-20 | Implement Android/iOS wrapper adapters only after packaging/orientation/budget/store approval; preserve shared-core parity from GPI-015. | DM-15–19; mobile approvals | `src/platform/{android,ios}`; `docs/target-matrix.md` | Device matrix demonstrates rule/content/save parity and explicit adaptations. |
[stderr] +| DM-21 | Integrate visual/audio loading, trigger routing, volume/mute/audio-focus, captions, reduced feedback, and platform interruption behaviour. | DM-07–09, 15–17, 20 as applicable | `src/platform/audio/`; `src/app/media/`; `PW-21-media.spec.*` | `PW-21` checks triggers once, mute/caption equivalence, unavailable audio, reduced feedback and cache fallback. |
[stderr] +| DM-22 | Add privacy/trust/release checks: provenance, licences, dependency scan, asset/package hashes, parser/size limits, CSP/static headers, no-secret check. | DM-03–10, 19 | `scripts/release-check.*`; `docs/{privacy,provenance,security}.md`; `tests/security/` | Release check rejects hostile content/save and incomplete creative record. |
[stderr] +| DM-23 | Create editorial operations, correction/withdrawal/rollback and player-support documentation. | DM-04–10, 18–22 | `docs/{editorial,content-release,player-guide,recovery}.md` | Tabletop correction and known-good rollback preserve active round/save. |
[stderr] +| DM-24 | Assemble quality evidence: core/content/persistence, accessibility, browser/device/offline/update, visual and audio review, performance and store-certification checklist. | DM-01–23; approved targets/budgets | test config; `docs/{quality-plan,test-matrix,release-runbook}.md`; `PW-24-release.spec.*` | CI-equivalent suite; `PW-24` primary start/save/resume path; manual matrix records approved gates. |
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Dependency summary
[stderr] +
[stderr] +```text
[stderr] +G design acceptance → DM-03 → DM-04/05 → DM-06 → DM-11/12 → DM-13 → DM-14 → DM-15/16/17 → DM-18
[stderr] +                     ├→ DM-07 → DM-09 ────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
[stderr] +                     └→ DM-08 ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┼→ DM-21 → DM-22 → DM-23 → DM-24
[stderr] +DM-10 ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
[stderr] +DM-19 (PWA) follows DM-14–18; DM-20 follows explicit mobile approval and DM-19.
[stderr] +```
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Account identity/remote sync, multiplayer/safety, live operations, purchases,
[stderr] +and seasonal content are excluded pending explicit product, privacy, safety,
[stderr] +cost, and operations decisions. No future task may copy or imitate reference
[stderr] +questions, branding, layouts, visual assets, or audio.
